# atrium-digital-convert — the published environment contract (atrium-project#60).
#
# Copy to `.env` and edit. Do not commit `.env` (it is gitignored).
#
# This file is the COMPLETE ledger: every variable the api image reads, at the
# default that is in the CODE. The operator-facing subset across all services is
# the table in the hub's docs/k8s_deployment.md; this file's layout is fixed by
# docs/templates/env.example.template in ufal/atrium-project.
#
# TAG LEGEND: [required] raises at startup without it · [secret] never a literal
# anywhere committed, use a k8s Secret · [operator] an ordinary deployment knob ·
# [algorithmic] changes what the service COMPUTES, not how it is deployed ·
# [build] read by compose/Dockerfile or baked at build time · [limit] a limit or
# setting (atrium-project#53): reported in GET /info, listed in service/README.md § Limits
#
# HOW THIS FILE REACHES THE PROCESS
#   docker compose  → delivered. docker-compose.yaml's `digital-convert-api` service
#                     declares `env_file: .env`, so everything below is injected into
#                     the container. PORT is ALSO named in its `environment:` block,
#                     because compose itself needs it for the `ports:` mapping.
#   Kubernetes      → NOT delivered. Use the manifest's own env: block. See
#                     ufal/atrium-project docs/k8s_deployment.md.
#   python -m service.api
#                   → NOT delivered. Nothing here calls load_dotenv(); export the
#                     values yourself:  set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#
# BLANK IS NOT UNIVERSALLY "UNSET". ALLOWED_ORIGINS is the trap: a blank value parses
# to an EMPTY origin list and blocks every browser request, where omitting the line
# gives you `*` — so it ships commented below, not blank.

# ── §0 Required before first start ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing. The converter needs no key, no model and no network. /describe's adjacent
# stages (§3) are optional: without them it answers from the converter alone.

# ── §1 HTTP surface ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [operator] Port the api service binds, and the port service/healthcheck.py probes
# inside the container. In Kubernetes, change `containerPort` in the same edit.
# (atrium-project#58)
PORT=8000
# [operator] Bind address. Leave at 0.0.0.0. service/healthcheck.py always probes
# 127.0.0.1 by design and never reads HOST, so 127.0.0.1 here gives a container that
# reports HEALTHY to every probe while being unreachable from outside it. This is the
# one value whose failure mode is silent.
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# [operator] CSV of CORS origins. Code default `*` (every origin). Ships commented so an
# operator who leaves it alone gets the real code default; uncomment to narrow it.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=*
# [limit] Canonical upload limit in megabytes, per uploaded part (the file and
# document_json). 50 is THIS repo's built-in (tool_limits.py, `upload_limit(50)`):
# born-digital PDFs with embedded images run larger than OCR text. Over it → 413
# limit_exceeded. Default: 50.
MAX_UPLOAD_MB=50
# [deprecated] Do not set. A byte-valued fallback kept working for one release for
# callers that already exported it (strategy §4.5); MAX_UPLOAD_MB wins whenever both
# are present. Listed commented-out so the contract is complete.
# MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=
# [operator] Path the container's own HEALTHCHECK probes. Change it only alongside
# the route itself.
# HEALTHCHECK_PATH=/health

# ── §2 Lifecycle ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [operator] Seconds uvicorn waits for in-flight requests after SIGTERM. A conversion
# takes seconds; a /describe with stages configured can take as long as the stages
# answer (STAGE_TIMEOUT_S per call). Raise it together with the deployment's grace
# period (terminationGracePeriodSeconds in k8s, see docs/k8s_deployment.md in the hub).
GRACEFUL_SHUTDOWN_S=20
# [operator] Root logger level for the `python -m service.api` start path. All
# services honour it identically (atrium-project#61).
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# [operator] Filesystem auto-reload. Development only — never in a deployment.
# RELOAD=false

# ── §3 Backing services (atrium-project#63) ─────────────────────────────────────
# The adjacent stages POST /describe calls (POST /reformat never calls them). Unset →
# the stage is reported `not_configured` and the assessment rests on the converter.
# In the AMČR deployment Temporal chains the stages and these stay unset.
# [operator] Base URL of an atrium-page-classification service (`/predict_document`).
# PAGE_CLASSIFICATION_URL=http://page-classification:8000
# [operator] Base URL of an atrium-ocr-postprocess service (`/score_record`; an older one
# is asked per page through `/process`).
# OCR_POSTPROCESS_URL=http://ocr-postprocess:8000
# [operator] The headless LibreOffice binary that converts legacy DOC/XLS. Unset → the
# first of `soffice`, `libreoffice` on PATH (the -digital and -api images ship it).
# Without one, DOC/XLS are refused with 501 (cause dependency_missing).
# LIBREOFFICE_BIN=soffice

# ── §4 Image / provenance ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [build] Image tag used by docker-compose: on release, para_config.txt's [tool] version
# WITHOUT the leading `v` (para_config.txt says `v1.1.0-beta`, GHCR carries
# `1.1.0-beta` -- atrium-project#69, roadmap B3). Read only by docker-compose.yaml.
ATRIUM_VERSION=dev
# [build] Baked at build time; stamped into paradata as runner_ref.
ATRIUM_RUNNER_REF=dev
# [build] Override either only if you publish under another name.
# ATRIUM_RUNNER_IMAGE=ghcr.io/ufal/atrium-digital-convert-api:dev
# ATRIUM_RUNNER_REPO=https://github.com/ufal/atrium-digital-convert
# [build] The uid docker-compose.yaml runs the containers as (`user: ${ATRIUM_UID:-10001}:0`);
# no Python here reads it. On Linux set it to your own uid -- `echo "ATRIUM_UID=$(id -u)" >> .env`
# -- so the container can write ./data, which a clone owns as you. (atrium-project#69, B6)
# ATRIUM_UID=10001
# [build] Correlation id copied verbatim into paradata `request_id`. Read ONCE from
# the process environment at import (atrium_paradata.py's module-level constants),
# so it identifies a batch run, not an individual HTTP request.
# ATRIUM_REQUEST_ID=
# [operator] The IRI (e.g. a ROR id) of the organisation that operates this deployment,
# recorded as the `agent` of every run's CreateAction (atrium-project#71). Unset, no agent
# is recorded; never set it to a processing account, which only reads and calls back.
# ATRIUM_RUN_AGENT=

# ── §5 Service knobs — operator ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Limits and settings (atrium-project#53) — every one of this service except MAX_UPLOAD_MB
# (§1), declared in tool_limits.py, reported with its current value in GET /info
# (`limits`; `limits_meta` names the variable and where the value came from), and listed
# in service/README.md's `## Limits` table. A malformed value stops the service at
# startup, naming the variable.
#
# [limit] Pages one document may have. Over it → 422 limit_exceeded. Default: 2000.
MAX_PAGES=2000
# [limit] Conversions the service runs at once; one more → 429 busy with Retry-After.
# Default: 2.
MAX_CONCURRENT_JOBS=2
# [limit] Seconds headless LibreOffice may take to convert one DOC/XLS. Over it → 422
# limit_exceeded. Default: 120.
LIBREOFFICE_TIMEOUT_S=120
# [limit] Seconds /describe waits for one call to an adjacent stage; over it the stage is
# reported `unavailable` and the request still succeeds. Default: 120.
STAGE_TIMEOUT_S=120
# [limit] POLICY: share of a PDF's text-bearing pages whose text layer is a prior OCR run at
# or above which the whole document is refused (422 ocr_text_layer); below it those pages
# are converted and flagged needs_ocr. Default: 0.5.
OCR_LAYER_DOCUMENT_SHARE=0.5
# [limit] POLICY (/describe): a page whose text layer decodes goes to OCR instead of NLP
# when the quality model calls more than this share of its scored lines Trash. Default: 0.5.
ROUTE_TRASH_SHARE=0.5
# [limit] The vendored reader's caps (text_formats.py, from atrium-ocr-postprocess — same
# names and defaults as there). Most a repeated ODF cell/row is expanded. Default: 100.
ATRIUM_TEXT_INGEST_ODF_REPEAT_CAP=100
# [limit] Most objects of one PDF page the shared reader scans to judge its text layer.
# Default: 20000.
ATRIUM_TEXT_INGEST_PDF_OBJECT_CAP=20000

# ── §6 Completeness ledger — algorithmic, deprecated, unreachable ────────────────
# [algorithmic] page-classification model revision /describe asks for (`all` = the ensemble).
# PAGE_CLASSIFICATION_VERSION=all
# [algorithmic] Categories per page page-classification returns to /describe.
# PAGE_CLASSIFICATION_TOPN=3
